to every child ListItem (an item may override it locally).&#x22; },\n  size: { type: '&#x22;small&#x22; | &#x22;medium&#x22;', default: '&#x22;small&#x22;', description: &#x22;Set on List, propagated to every child ListItem.&#x22; },\n  value: { type: &#x22;V[]&#x22;, default: &#x22;[]&#x22;, description: &#x22;Selection model, bind with [(value)]. Always an array, even for single selection.&#x22; },\n  multi: { type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;, default: &#x22;false&#x22;, description: &#x22;Enables multiple selection.&#x22; },\n  selectionMode: { type: '&#x22;follow&#x22; | &#x22;explicit&#x22;', default: '&#x22;follow&#x22;', description: &#x22;follow: selection tracks keyboard focus. explicit: select only via click/Space.&#x22; },\n  focusMode: { type: '&#x22;roving&#x22; | &#x22;activedescendant&#x22;', default: '&#x22;roving&#x22;', description: 'activedescendant keeps DOM focus on a host input (used by Autocomplete); the &#x22;focused&#x22; row is then exposed via data-active, not native :focus.' },\n}\"\n/>"],[1586,"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  variant: { type: '&#x22;primary&#x22; | &#x22;secondary&#x22;', default: '&#x22;primary&#x22;', description: &#x22;primary = soft/tinted fill; secondary = transparent background with a colored outline.&#x22; },\n  scheme: { type: '&#x22;sage&#x22; | &#x22;almond&#x22; | &#x22;pink&#x22; | &#x22;grey&#x22; | &#x22;yellow&#x22; | &#x22;cherry&#x22; | &#x22;indigo&#x22; | &#x22;cyan&#x22; | &#x22;success&#x22; | &#x22;warning&#x22; | &#x22;info&#x22; | &#x22;error&#x22;', default: '&#x22;sage&#x22;', description: &#x22;Semantic color palette.&#x22; },\n  size: { type: '&#x22;xs&#x22; | &#x22;sm&#x22; | &#x22;md&#x22;', default: '&#x22;md&#x22;', description: &#x22;Controls padding, radius, text size and the .tag-icon slot size. xsmall/small/medium are accepted aliases, kept for BEM parity — prefer the short forms.&#x22; },\n}\"\n/>"],[1627,"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  variant: { type: '&#x22;unique&#x22; | &#x22;multi&#x22;', default: '&#x22;unique&#x22;', description: &#x22;Color palette. A grouped item inherits its parent ToggleGroup's palette unless it sets its own.&#x22; },\n  size: { type: '&#x22;sm&#x22; | &#x22;md&#x22;', default: '&#x22;sm&#x22;', description: '&#x22;small&#x22;/&#x22;medium&#x22; accepted as legacy aliases.' },\n  iconOnly: { type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;, default: &#x22;false&#x22;, description: &#x22;Renders a square, icon-only pill.&#x22; },\n  pressed: { type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;, default: &#x22;false&#x22;, description: &#x22;Standalone Toggle only — two-way bindable pressed state.&#x22; },\n  value: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, description: &#x22;Grouped item only. Required — the widget's identity within the parent ToggleGroup's selection.&#x22; },\n}\"\n/>"],[1946,"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  withHandle: { type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;, default: &#x22;false&#x22;, description: &#x22;Shows the grip pill on the line.&#x22; },\n  &#x22;aria-label&#x22;: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, default: '&#x22;Resize panels&#x22;', description: &#x22;Accessible name of the separator. Override per handle when a group has several.&#x22; },\n}\"\n/>"],[1457,"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  workspaceId: { type: &#x22;string | null&#x22;, default: &#x22;null&#x22;, description: &#x22;The workspace shown; null is the list. A two-way model (workspaceIdChange).&#x22; },\n  uploadEndpoint: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, default: '&#x22;&#x22;', description: &#x22;The tus endpoint uploads go to. A relative path resolves against the configured backend.&#x22; },\n  queryName: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, default: '&#x22;_query&#x22;', description: &#x22;The query the preview web service renders a document for.&#x22; },\n  theme: { type: '&#x22;light&#x22; | &#x22;dark&#x22; | null', default: &#x22;null&#x22;, description: &#x22;dark turns the dark tokens on for the shell; otherwise it follows the page.&#x22; },\n}\"\n/>"],[1373,"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  workspaceId: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, description: &#x22;Required on <workspace-detail>. The workspace shown; changing it loads the other one.&#x22; },\n  uploadEndpoint: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, default: '&#x22;&#x22;', description: &#x22;<workspace-detail>: the tus endpoint uploads go to.&#x22; },\n  previewedDocumentId: { type: &#x22;string | null&#x22;, default: &#x22;null&#x22;, description: &#x22;<workspace-detail>: the document open in the preview. A two-way model, so the host can open one and is told when it changes.&#x22; },\n  queryName: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, default: '&#x22;_query&#x22;', description: &#x22;<workspace-detail>: the query the preview web service renders a document for.&#x22; },\n}\"\n/>"],[2054,"<TypeTable\n  type=\"{\n  wrap: {\n    type: &#x22;boolean&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;true&#x22;,\n    description: &#x22;Forwarded from @angular/aria/menu. Whether focus wraps from the last item back to the first, and vice versa.&#x22;,\n  },\n  typeaheadDelay: {\n    type: &#x22;number&#x22;,\n    default: &#x22;500&#x22;,\n    description: &#x22;Forwarded from @angular/aria/menu. Delay (ms) before the typeahead search buffer clears.&#x22;,\n  },\n  placement: {\n    type: &#x22;Placement&#x22;,\n    default: '&#x22;bottom&#x22; (root) · &#x22;right-start&#x22; (SubMenu)',\n    description: &#x22;Forwarded from PopoverDirective. Any @floating-ui/dom placement; flips/shifts on collision.&#x22;,\n  },\n  offset: { type: &#x22;number&#x22;, default: &#x22;4&#x22;, description: &#x22;Forwarded from PopoverDirective. Distance in pixels between trigger and menu.&#x22; },\n  class: { type: &#x22;string&#x22;, description: &#x22;Additional Tailwind classes, merged via cn().&#x22; },\n}\"\n/>"],[2112,"25% of the viewport"],[2115,"33% of the viewport"],[2111,"400px"],[2118,"50% of the viewport"],[2114,"520px"],[2117,"720px"],[2121,"75% of the viewport"],[2120,"960px"],[135,"A **collection** (the API calls it a *basket*) is a user-managed group of documents, persisted server-side\nthrough `UserSettingsStore`. `<collections>` renders the current user's collections as a list; the\n`AddToCollection` and `DeleteCollection` callables handle adding articles to one and removing one entirely."],[160,"A **label** is a free-text tag attached to a document, either **public** (shared, visible to every user) or\n**private** (visible only to the user who added it). `<multiselect-labels>` is the field that adds and removes\nthem on one article field; `EditLabels` is the dialog that shows the public and private fields together for a\nsingle document."],[36,"A **token** is a CSS custom property published by the design system — `--bg-primary-base`,\n`--font-primary-muted`, `--row-height-xs` — rather than a raw Tailwind utility or a literal colour. Every\n`galactik` component is styled exclusively through these tokens, so an application that declares them gets a\nconsistent look with zero component-level configuration."],[1350,"A *workspace* is a named set of documents that a user creates, fills by uploading files, shares with other\npeople and previews. The container API of `@sinequa/atomic` calls it a **container**; that word stays inside the\nlibrary, and everything you touch here says workspace."],[403,"A `category` axis, never `\"time\"` — this library ships no Chart.js date adapter, and setting\n`scales.x.type = \"time\"` without one compiles perfectly and throws at runtime. Bucket labels are resolved by\n`buildTimeline()` (a pure function, unit-testable without a chart), which also fills gaps: an empty bucket is\ndrawn flat at zero rather than skipped, so the shape of the series is never silently misrepresented."],[1818,"A `height` utility on the control cancels `field-sizing` outright. Bound the height with `minRows`/`maxRows` on\nthe wrapper instead of a fixed `h-*` class on the control in `auto` mode."],[440,"A bar, pie or doughnut chart, from the Chart.js entry point."],[877,"A bare `@if` around projected content does not carry the `slot` attribute the content projection matches on —\nwrap it in an `<ng-container slot=\"extra-actions\">` (as in the recipe above), not a bare `@if` directly around\nthe action."],[136,"A basket is the backend's name for a collection: a named list of document ids, stored per user. `Basket` (from\n`@sinequa/atomic-angular`'s models) is `{ name: string; ids?: string[] }` — the type every component on this\npage reads and writes."],[117,"A bookmark remembers one document; a **saved search** remembers a whole search state — the query text, every\napplied filter, the sort order — as the URL that reproduces it. `<saved-search-popover>` is the starred toggle\nthat saves or unsaves the *current* search in one click; `<saved-searches>` is the paginated list of everything\nthe user has saved."],[1505,"A bullet has no text, so on its own it says nothing to assistive technology — when the label next to it\nalready names the status, that is correct: the dot is decoration, and stays out of the accessibility tree. Set\n`aria-label` only when the dot is the *only* indication of the state, and it renders `role=\"img\"` with that\naccessible name."],[565,"A chip's identity is its **leaf filter**, not its value: a date distribution's two bounds can share one value\n(\"This year\" is `modified >= 2026-01-01`, \"Before this year\" is `modified < 2026-01-01`, differing only by\noperator), so tracking by value would make removing one chip drop both."],[469,"A cloud needs space: words that find no room are dropped rather than shown overlapping, and the count is\nsurfaced so the omission is never silent."],[578,"A collapsible accordion of facets for a sidebar or drawer, with keyboard navigation jumping directly between facet headers."],[57,"A collapsible app navigation panel, for the shell around pages like this one."],[1847,"A collapsible app navigation panel, with an automatic mobile drawer."],[908,"A collapsible metadata panel for a document preview — you provide the rows, the component owns only the collapsible shell and their two-column (key | value) layout."],[905,"A collapsible metadata panel to place above the preview."],[848,"A collapsible metadata panel with caller-projected rows."],[1509,"A color is never the only carrier of information (WCAG 1.4.1). Pair the bullet with a text label, or give it\nan `aria-label` when there genuinely is no label next to it. Do not put text inside a bullet either — its\nsize is fixed and content would be clipped; write the label as a sibling instead."],[1498,"A colored dot showing a status, category or priority next to a label — the dot half of Badge, without the content."],[1517,"A colored status dot, the undressed half of Badge."],[790,"A compatibility bridge for a legacy `Text[lang]Translation` syntax that predates Angular i18n — most\napplications never author strings in this format themselves, but the server still returns some. Impure by\ndesign: it re-evaluates on every `TranslocoService.langChanges$` emission, not only on a new input value, so a\nlabel already on screen updates when the user switches language without any component code reacting to it."],[1887,"A component projected inside `sidebarHeader`/`sidebarContent`/`sidebarFooter` reads the panel's own state by\ninjecting `SIDEBAR_REF` — the same token `SidebarTriggerDirective` itself resolves through."],[1964,"A confirmation prompt, an edit form, a notice that needs an explicit dismissal — each of those is a window\nthat has to sit above the rest of the page, trap focus while it is open, and hand a result back to whoever\nopened it. `Dialog` is that window, built on the native HTML `<dialog>` element (or a `[dialog]` attribute on\nany other host), and `createCallable`/`injectCallRef` is the typed call/result API most of this page teaches."],[481,"A controlled date facet, with a live selection"],[227,"A current/new/confirm password form that signs the user back in on success, so the session is never left stale — used both as the /login?mode=changepassword route and embedded in a profile panel."],[1224,"A custom \"Promoted\" badge"],[401,"A date aggregation's buckets, plotted as a stepped line with an optional drag-to-select brush — replacing an\n\\~800-line d3 timeline with Chart.js alone, plus a category axis and a small brush plugin."],[1976,"A declarative (non-callable) dialog, using every layout slot plus the three ways to open the same `<dialog>`\nreference."],[1613,"A directive that restyles the native `<button>` element, and a pressed/unpressed pill that works standalone\nor grouped into an exclusive or multi-selection toolbar."],[2188,"A disabled `<button>` receives no pointer events in most browsers, so nothing opens the tooltip. Put the\ndirective on a wrapper element, or use `aria-disabled=\"true\"` instead of `disabled`."],[1171,"A document can match a multi-term query without containing every term — `<missing-terms>` reads\n`article.termspresence` and shows the ones absent from this specific document, each one a link that re-runs\nthe search with that term required."],[1129,"A document's place in a hierarchy, as breadcrumbs that overflow into a dropdown."],[1110,"A document's place in a hierarchy, as clickable breadcrumb segments that navigate through an aggregation — and overflow into a dropdown when the container is too narrow."],[1206,"A dropdown listing the sort choices a tab or query configuration actually offers, resolved from the current result rather than passed in by hand."],[2039,"A dropdown of actions, a \"kebab\" row menu, a nested settings menu — `Menu` composes `MenuItem`s (with optional\nnested `SubMenu`s) inside `MenuContent`, wired to a trigger with `MenuTriggerDirective`. It is itself a\npopover — opening, positioning, dismissal and focus restoration all come from the same native Popover API\nPopover is built on, applied as a host directive, so there is no `<div popover>` wrapper to\nwrite yourself."],[1126,"A dropdown of the sort choices a tab or query configuration actually offers."],[1754,"A dropdown that behaves like a native `<select>` — keyboard navigable, `aria-selected`, popup positioned near\nthe field — but accepts option and trigger content of any shape. `SelectMenu` (`SelectComponent`) covers both\nsingle and multiple selection from one component."],[520,"A facet — \"Sources\", \"Authors\", \"Modified date\" — is one **aggregation** of a query's result, rendered so the\nuser can turn a bucket into a filter with a click. `<Aggregation>` picks and renders the right shape (a flat\nlist, a tree, or a date range) for a given column, and handles selecting, applying and clearing the filter for\nyou."],[568,"A facet lit from its own local selection state has to reconcile after a chip is removed elsewhere on the\npage — neither the value nor the object reference survives the round-trip (the store rebuilds entries by\nspreading them), so compare on `filterKey` instead:"],[602,"A fixed placement, ignoring available space"],[82,"A floating action bar that appears once the user has multi-selected documents — add to a collection, export, or attach to an AI assistant — backed by the shared SelectionStore."],[80,"A floating bar for acting on several selected documents at once."],[2097,"A footer with actions"],[1782,"A free-text field that turns what is typed into removable tags — comma or Enter adds one, Backspace removes the last, duplicates are ignored."],[1687,"A free-text field that turns what is typed into removable tags."],[965,"A full-page error state with an optional detail message read from the \"message\" query param, and a way back to a fresh sign-in attempt."],[984,"A full-page error state with an optional detail message."],[983,"A full-screen dimming overlay, shown and hidden through a service."],[957,"A full-screen dimming overlay, shown and hidden through BackdropService — not a settable input."],[1750,"A fully custom trigger"],[170,"A functional route guard that checks authentication, loads the principal, and redirects to change-password when a credentials session's password has expired."],[1947,"A group with no measurable size (a hidden route, `display: none`) cannot turn a pointer move into a\npercentage, and the drag is simply ignored until the group has a size again. Check that the group's parent\nactually has a height — a bare `<div>` with no height collapses the whole group to zero."],[1629,"A grouped item requires an ancestor `<ToggleGroup>` (or any `ngToolbar`) — `ToolbarWidget` resolves\n`inject(Toolbar)` through the regular element-injector hierarchy, so `<Toggle value>` items must be light-DOM\ndescendants of `<ToggleGroup>`, not children of some other wrapping component."],[1280,"A keyboard shortcut usually means three things to get right at once: comparing the right kind of key across\nkeyboard layouts, not stealing a keystroke a text field or another component needs, and keeping a help list\nthat does not drift from what is actually registered. `KeyboardShortcutsService` is one `keydown` listener, one\nregistry, and a `[keyShortcut]` directive for the common case — built to replace an older engine that could\nnot be made correct on a non-US layout."],[1560,"A keyboard-navigable ARIA grid shell for a list of rows that hold more than one focusable control — reach for it instead of List/ListItem in that case."],[1521,"A keyboard-navigable grid for rows that need more than one focusable control."],[1029,"A labeled light/dark switch for one ThemeStore scope, built on Signal Forms' checkbox contract."],[981,"A light/dark switch for a scope."],[1054,"A light/dark switch for a scope."],[1027,"A light/dark switch for the same scope."],[2048,"A menu entry that toggles a state cannot put a control (a checkbox, a switch) **inside** a `MenuItem`: a\n`menuitem` containing an interactive control is invalid ARIA, and it would leave that control out of the\nmenu's own keyboard navigation. The ARIA APG answer is for the item itself to carry the role and the\nstate — supported through `role=\"menuitemcheckbox\"`/`\"menuitemradio\"` plus a `checked` input, which also stops\nthe menu from closing when such an item is picked, so several options can be toggled in a row."],[980,"A menu listing every registered theme for a scope."],[1053,"A menu of registered themes, bound to a scope."],[1019,"A menu, opened from your own trigger content, listing every registered theme for a scope and switching it on click."],[2040,"A menu's items are not each individually tabbable: `Tab` leaves the whole menu in one step, and `↓`/`↑`/`Home`/\n`End` move a single \"active\" focus between items instead. This is the ARIA **menu** pattern, and\n`@angular/aria/menu` implements all of it — the roving focus, the keyboard navigation, and typeahead — so\n`Menu` only has to compose the pieces."],[532,"A missing aggregation is a misconfiguration (a typo'd `name`, an aggregation removed from the app's setup) —\nnot a state worth showing the user anything about — so it always disappears. A facet that genuinely resolves\nto zero items is a legitimate, often temporary state, so it stays by default and only disappears once you opt\nin with `hideWhenEmpty`. Two exemptions keep a facet the user can still act on regardless of that input: a\ndate facet (no \"resolved but empty\" state exists for it — see Pitfalls) and a facet currently\ncarrying an applied filter (hiding it would leave no way to clear that filter from the facet itself)."],[1090,"A mixed result — some terms corrected, others expanded — deliberately falls back to `suggestion`: it is the\nonly one of the three messages that does not assert a specific search behavior that may not actually have\nhappened for every term."],[2092,"A modal panel anchored to one edge of the viewport — the drawer pattern — built on the same native <dialog> as Dialog, with its own slide-in/out animation and scroll lock."],[2021,"A modal panel anchored to one edge of the viewport — the drawer pattern — sharing Dialog's tokens."],[2062,"A modal window with the same imperative call/result API, for content heavier than a menu."],[1845,"A native anchor styled as a navigation link, internal or external."],[1771,"A native checkbox styled as an on/off track-and-thumb toggle, with the same Signal Forms shape as Checkbox."],[1659,"A native checkbox wrapped in an accessible label, with an indeterminate visual state and Signal Forms integration."],[1689,"A native input wrapped in a styled flex container that drives its focus, disabled and read-only look purely from the input's own state, with optional icon slots and a character counter."],[1702,"A native radio input wrapped in an accessible label, grouped by a shared name and a derived selection signal rather than a container component."],[1805,"A native textarea wrapped like Input, with three height strategies and a rows-independent min/max bound for content-driven auto-sizing."],[1919,"A navigation panel that composes many of the same accessibility patterns."],[430,"A one-dimensional aggregation as a wrapping list of tags — the lightweight option."],[243,"A one-field form that requests a password-reset email — no router, no navigation, safe to drop into a dialog or a wizard step as-is."],[268,"A one-field reset-email request, safe to embed anywhere."],[149,"A paginated list of the user's collections, with add-to-collection and delete dialogs."],[129,"A paginated list of the user's saved collections (baskets), with an add-to-collection dialog and a delete confirmation — built on the shared ListPanel primitives."],[2052,"A panel that is not a `Menu` — a listbox of search results, a custom popover — can wear the same surface through the\nclass helpers the `Menu` itself is built from: `menuPanelVariants()` (rounded, shadowed, padded panel),\n`menuItemVariants()` (a row, with hover, active and disabled states), `menuContentVariants()` and\n`menuSeparatorVariants()`. They only return class names; the behaviour — roles, keyboard, positioning — stays yours."],[2098,"A panel with no visible title"],[1591,"A pastille apposed on another element — a counter or a status icon — rather than an inline chip."],[1516,"A pastille apposed on another element — a counter or a status icon."],[1637,"A people picker"],[1617,"A pill-shaped pressed/unpressed button, standalone or grouped into a segmented control built on @angular/aria/toolbar."],[2157,"A press on the host (`pointerdown`, `click`) closes the tooltip, and the focus that a press gives a button does\nnot open it again: only a keyboard focus does."],[1615,"A pressed/unpressed pill, standalone or as a segmented control built on @angular/aria/toolbar."],[1609,"A pressed/unpressed pill, standalone or grouped into a segmented control."],[32,"A pure Angular presentation library of tokens-only components — buttons, forms, overlays, navigation — for building Sinequa search UIs."],[1496,"A read-only inline chip for categorizing content, instead of a pastille glued to another element."],[693,"A recovery hook (`client.config.auth.recoverFromUnauthorized`) usually performs requests of its own. If one of\nthose comes back 401, the client calls the hook again — and a hook that returns the recovery already in flight\nwaits on itself, silently. Pass `noRecovery: true` on the requests your recovery makes, and have it refuse\nre-entry while a recovery is already running."],[770,"A request either goes through the atomic client (which handles it directly) or through `HttpClient` (which\nthese interceptors cover) — never both. Registering the client's own handling *and* these interceptors is\ntherefore correct, not a duplicate."],[1763,"A rich label that `fieldLabel` cannot express goes in a projected `.select-label` element, with\n`SelectLabelDirective` in the `imports` of the declaring component: the directive gives the element an id and the\nselect names the trigger and the list from it (the projected label wins over `fieldLabel`). Without the directive\nthe element is painted but is not part of the accessible name."],[1293,"A route held by a `RouteReuseStrategy` is not destroyed on navigation, so a `[keyShortcut]` on it stays\nregistered even though the page is no longer visible. Bind `[shortcutDisabled]` to whether the route is\ncurrently active."],[752,"A route or component subtree with its own client, stores and services."],[2053,"A row that is the current one is tinted like a hovered item: `data-active=\"true\"` for the Menu's own roving items and for\nthe options of an `@angular/aria` listbox (which mark the current row that way), `aria-selected=\"true\"` for a listbox written\nby hand following the APG."],[1046,"A scope is just a string key you choose (`\"application\"`, `\"main\"`, the id of a panel) — `ThemeStore` keeps one\nindependent theme/dark-mode pair per scope, so nesting or coexisting themes is a matter of using different scope\nnames, not a feature you configure."],[1733,"A search field styled like InputGroup, meant to sit inline among other form fields rather than standing alone as a pill."],[1683,"A search field styled to blend into a form."],[1647,"A search fires once the typed query, debounced, reaches `minLength` characters. While it is in flight the field's\nchevron gives way to a spinner and the rows of the previous search stay on screen — replacing them with a\n\"Searching…\" line made the list blink on every keystroke — so `searchingText` only shows when there is nothing\nto keep. Only a search that has come back (empty) may claim there is nothing, and a failed one says so in an\nalert row (`errorText`). The `loader` receives an `AbortSignal`: a newer query aborts the request of the older\none — hand it to `fetch`. The popup is a manual popover in the top layer, so a dialog's edges don't clip it."],[641,"A search rarely stays a plain text query. The user ticks \"PDF only\", expands a folder in a tree, picks \"last\nmonth\" — each facet renders one aggregation of the query's result, and clicking an item turns into a filter on\nthe next query. This section covers that whole loop: rendering a facet, applying and clearing its selection,\nand showing the user what is currently filtered."],[1196,"A search that fails still resolves to a `Result` — the request never throws — with the failure captured on\n`$error` instead. An empty `records` array is ambiguous by itself: it means \"the corpus matched nothing\" on a\nsuccessful request, and \"something went wrong\" on a failed one. Check `$error` first, always."],[1684,"A self-contained pill search field with clear and send controls."],[1723,"A self-contained search field — think an application's global search — with a leading magnifier icon and\nbuilt-in clear (×) and send controls, distinct from `SearchInput` which blends into a\nform alongside other fields."],[1715,"A self-contained, pill-shaped search field with a leading icon and built-in clear/send controls, meant to stand on its own rather than inside a form."],[2129,"A sheet still needs an accessible name with no heading in the design. `ariaLabel` provides it directly and\ntakes precedence over `labelledby` and over any projected title; `closeButton` floats a close affordance for a\nfull-bleed panel that carries no `SheetHeader` at all."],[2130,"A sheet that answers a question — pick a collection, confirm an export — opens imperatively and resolves,\nexactly like a callable dialog: `createCallable` takes any standalone component, and nothing in that path\nrequires a `<dialog>` element, so a `Sheet` works with it unchanged. Wire `end()` to `closeEnd` rather than to\nthe click that closes the panel — that is what lets the exit animation play before the component is destroyed."],[2025,"A short description on hover and keyboard focus, in the top layer, with the same selector as the @sinequa/ui one."],[2142,"A short description shown next to any element on hover and keyboard focus, placed in the top layer — the galactik replacement of the @sinequa/ui tooltip directive."],[359,"A Sinequa aggregation as a bar, pie or doughnut chart, on Chart.js — an optional peer dependency, from a separate entry point."],[6,"A Sinequa application typically layers three things: a **backend** (the search engine and its REST API), a\n**client** (`@sinequa/atomic`, which turns REST calls into typed queries and results), and a **UI layer**\n(this library) that renders that data as sign-in screens, facets, result lists and previews. Nothing here talks\nto the backend directly — every network call goes through `@sinequa/atomic`."],[893,"A Sinequa index can store more than one rendered form of a document — its **conversions** (a PDF-like page\nimage, a Markdown extraction, a multi-format bundle). `<preview-content>` resolves which conversion is active\nand swaps its whole rendering strategy (iframe vs. Markdown) based on it — this is not a cosmetic detail, the\nmarkdown branch skips the iframe and `<preview-actions>`'s search/highlights entirely."],[1711,"A single `Radio` exposes exactly `checked = model<boolean>(...)`, the structural shape `FormCheckboxControl`\nrequires — so `[formField]` binds one radio to one boolean sub-field, but `FormCheckboxControl` doesn't give a\nwhole group mutual exclusivity by itself. For an exclusive choice backed by Signal Forms, keep the shared-signal\npattern from the minimal example (or wrap the group behind a custom `FormValueControl<string>`)."],[1744,"A single- or multiple-choice dropdown built on the accessible @angular/aria combobox/listbox primitives, with a fully custom trigger and option rendering when the default chrome doesn't fit."],[1685,"A single- or multiple-choice dropdown over a fixed, synchronous options list."],[56,"A single- or multiple-choice dropdown, the other half of most forms."],[1681,"A single-line text field with icon slots and a character counter."],[1621,"A single-selection segmented control"],[53,"A small form: an `Input` bound to a signal, and a `Button` that opens a confirmation `Dialog` before\n\"submitting\" — the same `createCallable`/`injectCallRef` pattern the Dialog page\nteaches in full."],[1484,"A small pastille apposed on another element — a numeric counter or a status icon — glued on with your own positioning."],[77,"A starred toggle button on a document, and the paginated list of everything bookmarked."],[59,"A starred toggle button on any document, and a paginated list of the user's bookmarks — reopening one re-runs the query it came from to land back on the exact record."],[1575,"A static, read-only chip for categorizing content — a document type, an applied filter shown for reference, a status label."],[1515,"A static, read-only chip for categorizing content."],[991,"A tab bar generated from the Angular Router's own child-route configuration, with automatic overflow into a dropdown and optional per-tab result counts."],[982,"A tab bar generated straight from the router's child-route configuration."],[1001,"A tab shows no badge at all (not a `0` badge) unless its `queryName` matches the current result's query name;\nit is disabled only once the matched count is exactly `0` — in the visible bar and in the overflow menu alike."],[1793,"A tag is trimmed. An empty one is ignored, and so is a duplicate **whatever its case** — the first spelling stays."],[1584,"A tag the user can take away carries a `tag-remove` after its label: a real `<button>` (Tab to reach it, Enter or Space\nto activate it) named after the tag, with an `removed` event."],[2146,"A template as the content"],[1045,"A theme is a named set of CSS custom properties — one value per color role (`primary`, `background`,\n`destructive`, …), in a light and a dark variant. `ThemeStore` holds every registered theme and, for each\n**scope** you define, which one is currently active and in which mode."],[1846,"A thin styling layer over @angular/aria/tabs."],[1899,"A thin Tailwind styling layer over Angular's official @angular/aria/tabs primitives — roles, focus and keyboard navigation come entirely from Angular."],[393,"A time series with a drag-to-select range brush, on Chart.js — no d3, no date adapter, gap-filled buckets."],[374,"A time series with a drag-to-select range brush, on the same ChartCanvas foundation."],[441,"A time series with a drag-to-select range brush."],[617,"A toolbar listing the facets a user can filter on — one popover button per aggregation, with overflow handled by a \"More\" button."],[1883,"A trailing `Badge` is pinned to the end of an item and dropped automatically once the\nsidebar is icon-only — there is no room next to a bare icon for a pill."],[419,"A two-dimensional distribution — documents by source **and** by format, say — needs more than a list: a\nheatmap shows both axes at once, with colour standing in for count. `<Heatmap>` renders it as a CSS grid,\nwhich is what lets every cell and every axis label be a real, clickable, keyboard-reachable `<button>`."],[437,"A two-dimensional distribution as a CSS grid — no dependency, accessible, clickable axis labels."],[375,"A two-dimensional distribution on canvas, for matrices too large for the DOM."],[1519,"A user or entity, as a picture or initials, with an automatic fallback."],[1346,"A user-managed set of documents — listed, opened, uploaded into, shared and previewed — as Angular components, with a custom-element build for pages that are not Angular."],[622,"A vertical bar, for a sidebar layout"],[223,"A view being torn down as the router leaves the page, a save already in flight, a telemetry event — all of\nthem can reach the server moments later, on a cookie that has just been deleted, and answer 401. Nothing\nrecovers from those: `@sinequa/atomic` (2.3.2+) closes the recovery from a deliberate `logout()` until the\nnext successful authentication, and `signIn()` refuses to redirect away from an authentication screen. Without\neither, the audit event's 401 re-probed the session, found it gone, and replaced the \"signed out\" confirmation\nwith `/login?returnUrl=/logout` — signing back in then returned the user to the logout page."],[662,"Above 6 overflow filters, `<More>` itself grows a facet-name search box, independently of which container it\nrenders inside — a popover with many facets is otherwise as hard to scan as a sidebar with many facets."],[1091,"Action"],[868,"Add an app-specific action"],[1994,"Add the equivalent for the manual backdrop `<div>` too, if you stack `[dialog]` attribute hosts."],[773,"Adds Sinequa's audit metadata to a request body, for any request whose URL contains `api/v1` and whose body is\nJSON-serializable (skipped for `HttpParams` bodies). The `@sinequa/atomic` API functions already add this to\ntheir own requests; this covers the ones built directly on `HttpClient`."],[771,"Adds the current interface language to the request body as `ui-language`, read fresh from `TranslocoService`\non **every** request rather than captured once — the language changes while the application runs (the user\nmenus and the user-profile form call `setActiveLang`), and a request must carry the one in force when it is\nsent. `FormData` bodies get the field appended directly; a plain object body is cloned with the field added.\n`GET`/`HEAD` requests pass through untouched — they carry no body with the `fetch` backend."],[692,"Adopt `injectAtomicClient()` everywhere once a client is provided; do not mix free functions and a provided\nclient in the same application."],[507,"Aggregation"],[358,"Aggregation Chart"],[474,"Aggregation date"],[376,"Aggregation Heatmap"],[392,"Aggregation Timeline"],[438,"Aggregation values as a wrapping list of tags, sized by count."],[458,"Aggregation values packed into a compact spiral layout — large words centered, smaller ones tucked into the gaps, some rotated."],[444,"Aggregation values rendered as a wrapping list of tags sized by count — the lightweight default, with no layout algorithm and no canvas."],[319,"Alerts"],[1353,"All of them read the same `WorkspacesStore`, so a change made in one — a role changed from \"Manage access\", a\nstatus patched by the upload flow — shows in the others without anything being pushed."],[372,"Almost always a container with no resolved height — Chart.js sizes the canvas from its parent's box. Give the\nhost (or its wrapper) an explicit height, as the examples on this page do with `class=\"h-64\"`."],[613,"Also a regression to report, not expected — the component closes its own popover on `focusout` once focus\ngenuinely leaves the button and its panel (checked via `contains()` on the `relatedTarget`). A `null`\n`relatedTarget` — focus leaving the document entirely (alt-tab, browser chrome) — is the one case where it is\ndeliberately left open, so it survives a window switch."],[356,"Also deliberate — `api/v2/user-profile` requests are excluded so the caller (typically a form) can show the\nerror inline instead of as a transient toast."],[529,"Always hidden, unconditionally"],[2185,"Always in the top layer, above dialogs"],[521,"An **aggregation** is a bucketed count over one column of the result set — how many documents have each\nvalue of `docformat`, how many fall in each date range of `modified`. The server computes it alongside the\nresult records; `<Aggregation>` never computes it itself, only renders and lets the user filter on it."],[1162,"An `iconPath` renders an `<img>`; otherwise `iconClass` is applied to an `<i>` element."],[1891,"An `InjectionToken<SidebarRef>` a `<Sidebar>` provides for anything projected into it, exposing `collapsed`,\n`isMobile`, `expanded` (all `Signal<boolean>`) and `toggle()`/`open()`/`close()` — the last three branch on\n`isMobile()` automatically (desktop collapse vs. the mobile drawer)."],[2027,"An accessible dropdown or contextual menu built on @angular/aria — roving focus, typeahead, unlimited nested submenus, and checkable items with no interactive control inside a menuitem."],[2022,"An accessible dropdown/contextual menu with nested submenus and checkable items."],[2140,"An accessible dropdown/contextual menu, itself built as a popover."],[1537,"An accessible list of selectable rows built on @angular/aria/listbox, with composable slots for content lists, action menus and navigation lists."],[1520,"An accessible list of selectable rows, built on @angular/aria/listbox."],[1482,"An adjacent role/category label to pair with an avatar in a member row."],[627,"An aggregation becomes a filter button only if the app's JSON configuration says so (`position: \"left\" |\n\"both\"`, never `\"left\"` only in the bar) and the admin has not marked it `hidden`. Resolving that list is\n`AggregationsService.getAuthorizedFilters` — the bar, `<more-button>` and `<aside-filters>` all call through it,\nso the three surfaces never disagree on which facets exist."],[328,"An alert is a saved query the server re-runs on a schedule — a frequency, the weekdays it repeats on, a time of\nday. `<Alerts>` lists, reorders and deletes them; `AlertForm` opens the dialog that creates or edits one."],[48,"An Angular 22 workspace with Tailwind CSS v4 already set up. `@sinequa/galactik` declares three peer\ndependencies — install them alongside it:"],[800,"An Angular route resolver that supplies the application's default query name to a route with no explicit one."],[1867,"An app navigation panel — collapsible to an icon rail on desktop, a native-dialog drawer below the mobile breakpoint — with no rail and no nested submenus."],[1242,"An application customizes its behavior mostly through the `general` object of its JSON configuration (a\ntop-level `general` key, or a `general` customJSON side-file) — read once through `AppStore.general()`. This\npage is the one place that lists every key of `general.features`/`general.feedback` **and says which ones a\nconsumer actually checks**, since a name in the type is not a promise that anything reads it."],[2179,"An arrow by default (`[tooltipArrow]=\"false\"` removes it)"],[1130,"An article field as a row of tags, and the icon identifying which source or collection it came from."],[744,"An audit event fired in the moments after a logout can land on the deleted session cookie, answer 401, and\nre-trigger `signIn()` — signing the user back in to a login form they deliberately left. `bootstrapApp` refuses\nrecovery for `api/v1/audit.notify` specifically, and for any request while a sign-in is already in flight (a\nrecovery that waited on its own in-flight sign-in would never settle). Both guards are already built in; if you\nsee this with a different endpoint, mark that request `noRecovery: true` rather than trying to special-case it\nhere."],[98,"An automatically populated, paginated list of the user's past searches — the same shape as saved searches, with nothing to save explicitly."],[1631,"An editable combobox for debounced backend search with multi-selection — labels, filter facets, people pickers — where picked values render as removable chips inside the field."],[2075,"An element with a `popover` attribute renders in the browser's **top layer** — above everything else, no\n`z-index` required — and is shown/hidden by the browser itself: native focus handling, `Escape`-to-close and\nclick-outside dismissal all come from the platform. `PopoverDirective` adds what the platform does not:\ncomputed placement relative to a trigger, collision-aware repositioning, and a couple of small ergonomics the\nraw attribute leaves to you."],[582,"An explicit, developer-chosen facet list"],[345,"An HttpInterceptorFn that turns a failed HttpClient request into a toast for the status codes worth telling the user about, without wrapping HttpClient itself."],[545,"An inline object literal on `[aggregation]` — `[aggregation]=\"{ ...agg, display: label }\"` — is a **new\nreference on every change-detection pass**, and any reference change reseeds the whole instance (discarding\nload-more pages and open tree nodes). It also fails to compile: the raw `Aggregation` type from\n`@sinequa/atomic` has no `display` field, so the literal trips the excess-property check."],[1672,"An on/off toggle with the same Signal Forms shape as Checkbox."],[1680,"An on/off track-and-thumb toggle."],[2019,"An overlay is anything that renders above the rest of the page and captures focus or dismissal on its own\nterms: a modal dialog, an edge-anchored sheet, a dropdown menu, a floating popover. `@sinequa/galactik`'s\noverlays share the same scrim tokens (`--scrim-base`, `--blur-xs`) and, wherever the platform allows it, the\nnative top layer — so none of them need an application-level `z-index` to stack correctly above ordinary\ncontent."],[1728,"Angular hoists a `slot=\"trailing\"` marker onto a block only when that block has a single root node. Putting the\nmarker on an element that is itself inside an `@if`/`@for`, or beside a `@let`, breaks the hoist (the compiler\nreports `NG8011`) and the content lands in the default slot instead. Put the marker on an `<ng-container>`\nwrapping the whole block:"],[1755,"Angular Signal Forms recognizes a component as a form control when it exposes a `value` model matching the\n`FormValueControl<TValue>` contract. `SelectMenu` implements it through its own `value` model, so `[formField]`\nworks exactly like it would on a native input — no adapter needed."],[1920,"Another @angular/aria-backed composite widget, for selecting rows instead of switching panels."],[1558,"Another @angular/aria-backed composite widget, for switching between panels instead of selecting rows."],[1535,"Another component driven entirely by keyboard interaction, this one via @angular/aria."],[1951,"Another panel-composition component, collapsible rather than resizable."],[1175,"Another per-document component — where it sits in a collection hierarchy."],[1163,"Another small, configuration-driven display component."],[1232,"Another small, configuration-driven display component."],[1823,"Answer one question as a signal — is the viewport narrower than the md breakpoint? — for structural choices CSS cannot express."],[726,"Anything calling a **free function** (`fetchQuery()`